uccess","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer correctly says the sponsor/partner bears the economic shortfall under its contractual cost-assumption arrangement, which covers the first key point. It gets the second requested fact wrong. The key point says the platform adviser still owes the fund its promised expenses if the partner fails to pay. The answer never mentions the platform adviser. Instead it says the fund itself may still owe service providers and would have a claim against the sponsor. That misidentifies the backstop obligor. It also omits that fixed costs can make a small fund unprofitable. It does at least frame the outcome as a contractual allocation, not a universal shareholder obligation.\"}","ttft_ms":1887,"type":"result","duration_ms":3605,"uuid":"c337952d-2c55-4100-ad2e-518b71a19059","ttft_stream_ms":1019,"time_to_request_ms":47,"first_content_frame_ms":1019,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
